d-222055e2893b" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671151 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=5.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 5 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =5 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =5 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =5\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =5 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 5 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(5 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{5+C}{1} \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5 + e^{- x}.\n$$" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671152 1080 "6 - 2 e^{- 6 x}" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671152 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671152 1083 #uuid "8822c766-03e4-5ba0-85d8-a63cdcfbd8b7" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671135 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671145 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671148 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186671160 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671153 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139538657 175