egin{aligned}e^{3 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y) & =e^{3 x}\\cdot 18 \\\\ e^{3 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3 e^{3 x}y & =18 e^{3 x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{3 x}) & =18 e^{3 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{3 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18 e^{3 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{3 x} & =18\\left(\\frac{1}{3} e^{3 x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{3 x} & =6 e^{3 x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 6 e^{3 x}\\right) e^{- 3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(6 e^{3 (0)})+C}{(e^{3 (0)})} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6 - 2 e^{- 3 x}.\n$$" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671168 1080 "5 + e^{- x}" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671168 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671168 1083 #uuid "e03e3cb6-cb28-5eb3-94cf-3bfc038afaa7" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671169 1080 "7 - 3 e^{- 6 x}" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671169 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671169 1083 #uuid "e3d1d641-b783-502e-aea7-744475d60287" 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671170 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671142 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671170 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671172 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671170 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538657 17592186045443 true] [17592186671170 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(1\\right)y=6,\\quad y(0)=4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{